WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:06.610
Let's go today to our caller from the two
five zero area code.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.360
Who's calling today from two five zero eight
seven Flemington's Asherman.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.290
I'm calling from Mary.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.230
Calling from Santa Victoria.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.230
Yes.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.130
You know where that is?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.779
Just a couple hours north of Seattle, OK.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:22.069
A couple hours north of Seattle.

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:24.329
What's going on today?

00:00:24.329 --> 00:00:26.369
I should have a quick question for you.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:28.479
I'm not cricket, as I say, but.

00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:34.620
So I think that you're probably aware, too,
that led to the eviction crisis is over pretty

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.460
soon here, probably in the next couple of
months, if not the next month.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.460
Yes.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.989
And I was wondering what you think of strategically
withholding rent as a tactic and how do you

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:50.860
think that would pan out in the US or how
effective do you think that would be?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.600
So I've actually I'm glad you're asking this.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.100
I've talked about, you know, I've done a bunch
of segments and there's one in particular

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:02.190
about types of activism where I've said, you
know, calling your representatives is great.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.460
Signing petitions online.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.500
I don't think it really does anything.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:14.850
But that activism tactics that may get more
attention would be mass rallies in urban centers,

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:20.409
strategic defaults of debt of different kinds,
which could include coordinated nonpayment

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:26.120
of mortgages, coordinated nonpayment of rent,
et cetera.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:32.130
I think the complexity right now is it wouldn't
just be activism.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:37.520
Like there's 32 percent of people were unable
to pay their entire mortgage or rent on July

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.729
1st.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:44.579
So what we're talking about is an actual economic
crisis in which a third of the country wasn't

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:47.409
able to fully make their July first payments.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:53.090
And then adding on top of that, another element
of this happening strategically during a time

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.310
when there may be an extended eviction moratorium
or there may not.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.460
It's unclear.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.049
They're talking about it, but it's not clear
a deal is actually going to get done.

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:04.909
So it's extremely speculative.

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:07.039
What what would happen in this particular
case?

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:12.060
The idea for people to understand of saying
nobody pay your mortgages, nobody pay your

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.060
rent?

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.030
Is that if everybody really did it?

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.720
And of course, everybody would never do it.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.360
There's a huge part of society that would
say, I'm fine.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.920
I'm not going to get involved in this.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.120
I'm not going to hurt my credit or whatever.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.280
But if a large enough portion of society withheld
mortgage and rent payments, you would instantly

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.520
cripple the financial industry with a massive
liquidity crisis.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:38.090
It would probably force the government to
have to, in the short term, put in a crazy

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.840
amount of money to keep these financial institutions
afloat.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.130
And the idea would be it would bring stakeholders
to the table to actually negotiate some of

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.080
the change that people people want.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.830
Now, agreeing on what the change people want
is is a whole other issue.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.030
And Ben brings complexity.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.340
But it's an interesting idea.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:03:00.830
I don't know what adding a strategic default
on top of an existing eviction and foreclosure

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.830
crisis

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.900
would would really do a potential one.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.560
But it's it's a very interesting question.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:12.160
Yeah, I think, like quickly, like I think
you would you would pan out a lot, whereas

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.740
in Canada where there is a little bit more
of a social net for people.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:21.060
But I think in America, I think where I don't
know if the socialist is quite there.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:27.070
So this kind of I think the point of view
on it would be a little more positive in certain

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.780
places versus other places.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:29.780
Right.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.190
That's I was asking you how you thought it
would pan out of the U.S.. Yeah.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.400
I really appreciate your son.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.810
I mean, listen, if it happened, if you had
a significantly coordinated mortgage and rent

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:44.690
default in the United States, it would immediately
become a hyper politicized where it would

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:53.490
be attacked by the right as just grifter,
lazy people on the left who don't want to

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.700
pay their bills and so on and so forth.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:01.620
The left would likely hail them as doing something
really good in order to inspire change potentially

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.810
at their own economic peril.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.910
And it would become honestly, just like everything
else, where it would become hyper partizan.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.390
And I don't know how far we would get with
it.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:11.390
Unfortunately.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.150
Yeah, fair enough, I agree with you there.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.760
All right, my friend, thank you for the call.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:17.760
Very interesting question.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.419
I appreciate it.

